Votes

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:28.660
Huh?

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:33.670
A Hat, Ice, and a Princess

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.340
Itsuki's a perfect fit for
the princess role, isn't she?

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.100
Well, that's only natural for Ittsun.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:41.180
Marumi   Rin   Itsuki   Fusako

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:41.180
Princess
Role

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.470
The vote was nearly unanimous.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.560
Yes, I need to live up to everyone's expectations.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.480
So, what is this play you're all in?

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:00.180
Um, it's a story called "The Lady in the Tower."

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.740
Long ago, the princess of a certain nation

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.120
received a mysterious power
from a witch of the lake.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.080
Whenever she said, "I wish this would happen,"

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.130
the moment her words reached another's
ears, they would become reality.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.880
At first, the king and queen were happy.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.390
But one day, after a lion appeared in their
hall, the princess was locked away

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.920
in a tower, where no one could hear her words.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.150
A long time passed,

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:38.570
and a prince from a far-off land heard a
rumor of the princess and came for her.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.650
The prince stood before her tower and said,

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:47.990
"I long to see your wishes granted once more."

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.000
"I no longer have any wishes to be granted,"

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:58.920
the prince heard the princess's faint voice reply
from behind the firmly closed doors.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:04.840
When the prince approached the door
to try and hear the princess more clearly,

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.640
lightning struck the tower.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:14.730
The prince hurried inside, but no one was there.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:23.490
"She must have wished to go to heaven,"
lamented the king and queen.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:28.830
However, the prince had heard her final words.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.830
"I wish I could disappear."

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.080
What a sad story.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.130
It's pretty heavy for middle schoolers.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.050
An imprisoned princess...

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.380
Ah, I'm feeling a surge of inspiration!

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.720
The princess's costume should use a pannier
for volume to make it really showy.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.850
Add plenty of gathers,

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.100
and about eight meters of frills on the skirt...

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.100
Wow...

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.020
What about the prince?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.480
Who cares? The prince can come later.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.390
Add a braid to the chest,
and frills on the sleeves...

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.020
It's done!

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.440
How does it look, Itsuki?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.190
Well...

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.360
Not bad!

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.150
It's good.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.070
This will definitely look good on you, Itsuki.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.910
Yes, I think it's great.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.160
Really?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.490
All right!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.910
Then time to start making it!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.920
Lace & Fringe

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.920
Bargain Sale

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.310
Wow, that's a really beautiful dress!

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.390
It's finally come together...

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.560
I bet it'll look really good on
Itsuki when she wears it.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.850
You think so?

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.520
There's some string in your bangs...

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:42.780
What's wrong?

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.700
Oh, sorry. My forehead looks really silly.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.030
I'll throw out the trash, so you guys go on ahead.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.040
Oh, I need to go return the class logbook, too.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.420
Faculty Room

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:04.130
Sorry I'm late...

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.220
Hey.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.560
U-Um, it appears the stars led me here again...

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.560
Could you close that?

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.230
Oh.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.110
Minato, are you always here?

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.110
Here?

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.110
Um...

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.870
This place is at school, right?

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.240
What's school?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.790
Maybe I really am dreaming.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.250
Even though classes just ended...

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.750
Dreaming?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.750
Dreams, huh?

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:46.510
Then would that make me a resident
of your dreams, Subaru?

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.210
Do you think I'm only here while you dream?

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.560
Please don't tease me like that.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.480
Why not? I'm always here.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.060
This is the only place I know.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.640
Huh?

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.480
The princess...

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:07.490
Hmm?

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:10.990
You're kind of like the princess.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.740
What are you talking about?

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.620
Don't you want to leave this place?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.620
Why? What would doing that accomplish?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.710
Accomplish?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.670
Isn't there anywhere you'd like to go?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.090
Who knows?

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:33.550
If this is your dream,
then you only need to wake up.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.310
I wonder where I'd end up then?

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.230
Or perhaps, together with your dream...

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:40.850
No!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:43.850
No...

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.980
You can't say that.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:48.950
I'm joking.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.320
Huh?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.160
Is someone there?

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.580
Itsuki?

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.920
Oh, sorry! Were you changing?

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.880
Huh? Oh, no, don't worry about it.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.550
Um, earlier—

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:13.180
I was sort of hoping you'd still be here.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.430
Huh?

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.580
Hey, want to go for a drive?

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:24.480
Wow, until just recently, you could
barely climb above the clouds.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:27.020
I was practicing, and I just found myself here.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.900
You came this high just practicing?

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:32.950
Yeah, I wondered how far I could fly,
and I just kept going...

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.240
Sounds just like you.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:41.000
The president says that as we gather
engine fragments, our powers grow.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.420
I wonder if we can fly even higher.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.880
It's like we're having a dream.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.750
Itsuki, below!

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.260
A shooting star!

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.340
Did you make a wish, Itsuki?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.220
No.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:56.890
Huh?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.890
I don't have any wishes.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:03.060
I try not to think about things like that.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:08.060
Doing whatever I wanted would only
cause trouble for someone else.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:13.240
I don't want to hurt anyone else by being selfish.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.240
Itsuki...

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:19.120
When I was little, I was a real tomboy.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.540
I could do anything. I could go anywhere.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:27.080
As a child, that's what I believed.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.500
That's dangerous, Itsuki! Come down here!

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.670
Come up here, too.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.420
I can see our house.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.720
I thought that if I tried,

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.640
I could even fly.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:43.890
But...

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.390
I was wrong.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.070
You were there! Why couldn't you stop her?

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.280
I'm sorry.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:00.950
Oh, dear, what will we do if it scars?

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:02.330
I'm sorry.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:07.960
My parents blamed my brother, but I'm
sure he was already blaming himself.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.880
I hurt everyone by being selfish.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:16.760
I felt that this scar was a punishment,
warning me against that.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.030
So that's why you keep your bangs?

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.530
It's strange.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.530
I don't think I've ever told anyone that.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.050
Sorry about earlier.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.370
It's okay.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.080
Hey, you two...

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.920
Can I ask a favor, while you're there?

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.630
An engine fragment has appeared.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.930
You really found a fragment?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.730
I can't see it anywhere.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:12.060
My meteor shower forecast is updated daily.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.150
I got called back when I was on
my way home, thanks to that.

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:19.030
Not to mention, he says he found one,
but he doesn't know where it is.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:22.990
Even if we can't find its position, if we can
pinpoint its momentum, we'll be fine.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.370
I don't get it.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.490
We're bound to the fragment by fate.

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:31.790
Even if we can't pin down its position,
we may be able to call it toward us.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:32.630
There.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:37.960
It's the principle of leverage.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.550
We'll draw the fragment toward us,
using you two as a fulcrum.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.840
Are you sure this is all we need to do?

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.930
Let's try it.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.430
If we have to do this, then...

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.520
The president's turning weird colors?

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.780
It means they captured the fragment.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:00.280
Keep it up!

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:08.990
Itsuki, wait!

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.370
Subaru... No, Itsuki?

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.250
You're going a bit too hard...

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.960
He's gonna turn into boiled octopus!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.460
I've got a bad feeling.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.570
What's going on?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.900
A huge takoyaki?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.150
Orange sorbet?

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:43.900
It looks delicious.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:44.410
Hmm?

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:45.950
Crushed almonds?

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:47.660
Chocolate chips?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.370
Huh? What's that?

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.830
It's a super huge marble cake.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.410
Milk gelato!

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.130
Itsuki!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.390
Uh, lemon sherbet?

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.850
Caramel ice cream.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.100
Milk tea flavor.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.180
What's this?

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.810
A sea of rock candy?

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.560
It looks like a planet, but this is...

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.310
They're beads of ice. It's a ring!

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.440
There are so many beads of ice,

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.320
from far away, they look like a giant saucer.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.160
This is a ring?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.030
Itsuki, where are you?

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.950
Sorry, I got separated.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.490
For now, let's make sure everyone's safe.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.750
A planet with rings?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.830
Which means this is...

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.170
Saturn?!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.840
Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars,
Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus...

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.840
I see. So this is the sixth planet.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:51.180
So our attempt to draw the fragment toward us
drew us toward the fragment instead.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.770
That's such bull.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.140
No, by my theory, it's possible.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.270
I meant your plan is bull!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.940
The power in the fragments is even more incredible.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.110
And so is your own power.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.400
I wonder if I went too far.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.940
You aren't at fault, Ittsun.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.950
Good grief, you're a troublesome lot.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:15.870
Horned Cape!

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.080
You came this far?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.290
Hah! You're the ones who brought me here.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.210
Hitchhiking isn't fair!

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:26.630
Now that I've come this far,
I'll just take the fragment.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:30.470
What do we do?

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:33.970
Isn't it obvious? We capture it first.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:37.020
Think we can go back after we do,
like we did on the Moon?

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.230
Exactly.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.150
Wait, you mean there really is one?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.400
I know! The meteor shower forecast!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.780
All the implements are in our club room.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.940
Guess we'll have to search the hard way...

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:51.700
By the way, the width of
Saturn's ring is over 70,000 km.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:52.910
70,000 km?

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.370
About five Earths wide.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.790
What?!

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:58.910
Then why don't we set up
a magic circle like this?

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.420
It'll tell us where Ittsun and Subaru are,

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.920
and if we're lucky, we might
pick up the fragment, too.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.920
Yes. That's more effective than
trying to fly around this space.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.930
It's a triangle, not a five-point star.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.230
So that's where those two are?

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:23.270
This magic circle must be
as wide as three Earths.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:23.980
That's huge!

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.230
They're way too far away!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.860
We caught it even as we were
talking about it. How lucky!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.870
So, what now?

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.240
The magic circle's synchro-mesh

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:42.000
will use the fragment's power to
adjust us into the right position.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:42.580
Huh?

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.880
Meaning what?

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.460
I mean the fragment will pull us in, toward it.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:52.760
Say that earlier!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.800
All right, it's going well.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:57.560
Meaning it's just about time for...

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.890
I won't let you do that.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.980
I knew you'd show up!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:20.500
Everyone?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.250
Subaru, Itsuki, are you all right?

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.130
Thank goodness the ring is thin...

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:27.090
Oh, what about the fragment?

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.340
We lost sight of it again.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.460
Isn't that it?

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:33.180
No, that's different.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:36.850
When objects of large size and
density enter Saturn's ring,

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.560
they form unique patterns.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:41.930
On Earth, they apparently call
those patterns "propellers."

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.480
Then if we search for those patterns...

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.560
It takes several days for a visible pattern to form.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:48.570
That long?

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.860
Then we'll have to...

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.740
Huh? We'll have to what?

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.070
Nothing. Forget it.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:58.370
What is it?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.740
Itsuki, you thought of something, right?

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.460
What did you mean by "we'll have to"?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.580
No, we can't do that. It's dangerous...

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.130
We're used to danger.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.260
Please, Itsuki!

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.260
Everyone, follow me.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.270
We're going to charge into the ring!

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.400
Yes! Charge into it!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.690
The ring's going to break!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:37.570
No, don't worry. The ring flows like a river.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.410
The ripples we cause will soon disappear.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.080
One more time.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:42.830
Again?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.540
We have to do it until we
find it, or there's no point.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.330
Itsuki!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:50.130
Jeez... We're in this now, so we
might as well see it through!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.230
Again!

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:28.580
I can't believe I lost sight of the fragment.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:32.840
What?

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.340
Was there something there just now?

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.540
Look, over there.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.510
There's something there that isn't ice.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.850
They made use of its different mass?

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:49.900
We found it!

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:52.560
It's the engine fragment!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.690
That guy's planning to steal it from us!

00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.280
<i>I don't want to lose.</i>

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:29.310
We captured it!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.400
Damn it... How rough do you people get?

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:40.150
Your forehead's red.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.740
I'm surprised.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.530
I never knew you were the bold type, Itsuki.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.910
Yeah. I'm sorry, everyone.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:48.750
It's nothing to apologize for.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:51.710
But I caused problems for everyone...

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.210
You didn't cause problems.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:55.380
No, even if you did, it's fine.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.050
Right, Aoi?

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.050
Huh? Yeah, that's right.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.220
You can cause as much trouble for us as you like.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.050
How generous.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.760
Well, it goes both ways.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.390
Thank you, everyone.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:12.520
If you hadn't mentioned your scar,
I wouldn't have noticed it at all.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:17.770
Yeah. Maybe I was thinking about it too much...

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.610
We stabilized the fragment.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.660
Bid farewell to Saturn.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:36.290
That was "Midwinter's Sun" by Class 1-3.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.290
We're up next.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:42.920
Next, in five minutes, Class 1-1 will
be performing "The Lady in the Tower."

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.800
And then, the prince rescued
the princess from the tower,

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.260
and they both lived happily ever after.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:42.920
Huh?

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:45.300
Wasn't it supposed to be a sad story?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:49.600
We suggested in class that we
should give it a happy ending.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.350
Everyone else agreed.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.560
The prince ought to save the princess, after all.

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.110
Still, I'm more surprised by this.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:03.280
You actually wanted to play the
prince's role, huh, Itsuki?

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:06.620
Thank you for letting me have my way.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:09.120
Now, come on out, Princess.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:10.580
Yeah, but still...

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.460
I can't do this!

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.170
Please...

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.840
Will you take this hand of mine?

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.510
This is my wish.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:27.010
I-If you wish it from the heart,

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:30.600
then it will be my wish, as well.

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:36.980
They're both perfect.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.400
They're beautiful, aren't they?

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.910
To Be Continued

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.540
You see, when I looked up

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:06.930
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:16.640
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:25.610
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:22.980
...my daily life...

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:35.370
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:37.250
"Can I fly?"

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:41.460
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:47.090
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:56.770
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:56.770 --> 00:23:01.400
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:05.900
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:11.240
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:15.950
sometime after school

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:23.380
Subaru, you looked really
good as the flower spirit.

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:26.340
Your bamboo shoot was also cool, Nanako.

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:29.760
Sprouting your face out of the ground
was an incredible performance.

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:31.720
Next episode:
Flower of Awakening.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.680
Huh? Was that Minato?
